shwanathaya Namah\\\\\\\"\\\"}]\\n26:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"10\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Trust: Shri Vimal Parshwanath Shwetambar Jain Tirth, Vaniyawad, Post: Chhani, District: Vadodara, State of Gujarat, India. Phone number: 0265-2432858\\\"}]\\n27:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"11\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"The Fourth Birth - Kiranaveg and the Fierce Serpent Kaldarun: When his lifespan in the heavenly realm came to an end, the soul of Marubhuti was born as a son to King Vidyudveg and Queen Tilakavati in the city of Tilakapuri, on Mount Vaitadhya in the Sukachchh Vijay region of Mahavideh Kshetra. On reaching youth, he married a maiden named Padmavati; after his coronation, Vidyudveg himself took diksha and, through supreme spiritual practice, attained liberation (moksha).\\\"}]\\n28:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"12\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"A son named \\\\\\\"Dharanveg\\\\\\\" was born to King Kiranaveg. Once, Shri Vijaybhadracharya arrived there. Upon hearing just one of his sermons, King Kiranaveg was filled with detachment (vairagya). He immediately handed the kingdom to his son Dharanveg, and King Kiranaveg, together with Queen Padmavati, took diksha.\\\"}]\\n29:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"13\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Muni Kiranaveg practiced severe austerities, wandering through forests and mountains. The soul of Kamath, having completed his span of life in hell from a previous birth, was reborn in that very forest as the fierce serpent Kaldarun. He bit Kiranaveg, who had been Marubhuti in an earlier life. Poison spread through the muni's entire body. Though both their bodies had changed, one grew ever more equanimous while the other's hatred grew ever more intense. Muni Kiranaveg let go of attachment to the body and remained steadfast in dharma-dhyana (righteous meditation), and so his body became free of the sensation of pain. Even when there is pain in the body, it has no effect whatsoever on the soul and the mind - and because of this, no trace of distressed thought (artadhyana) arises from the pain.\\\"}]\\n2a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"14\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"The Fifth Birth - Heaven and Hell: Muni Kiranaveg, who had been Marubhuti, died in a state of pure meditation and was reborn as a god in the twelfth heaven, while the serpent died and went to hell. One soul enjoyed divine pleasures for countless years, while the other suffered the terrible torments of hell for countless years. One soul continues to bind auspicious karma, while the other continues to bind inauspicious karma. As long as a soul remains unmindful, the binding of inauspicious karma continues unabated. Therefore, we have a particular need to remain vigilant. To break the chain of inauspicious karmic bonds, one should apply the remedies described in the Panchsutra, such as dushkritagarha (repentance for wrongdoing) and so forth.\\\"}]\\n2b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"15\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Blessed indeed is the birth of those who have been granted the vision of Parshwa; great is the merit of those who have found a place at the feet of this wish-fulfilling gem! Even we, who are humble and possess nothing, have gained fame and good fortune through this name; every longing has come to its fulfillment since we found this life-giver!!\\\"}]\\n2c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"16\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Hymn of Praise to Shri 108 Parshwanath: What a wondrous \\\\\\\"Manmohana\\\\\\\" (heart-enchanter) you are, captivating the hearts of all devotees; none can match the \\\\\\\"Jotingda,\\\\\\\" beholding whom the heart sways with joy. Listen, O Lord \\\\\\\"Shankhala\\\\\\\"! Destroy my enemy karmas. O Lord Shankheshwara! I beseech you, protect me! Protect me!! O dark-hued one (Sanvara).\\\"}]\\n\"])</script></body></html>","rscData":"","segmentData":{"/_tree":"","/_full":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug":"","/$d$lang/tirtha":"","/$d$lang":"","/_index":"","/_head":""},"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x